# A screen's route data is the live bindings its view reads, each keyed by
# its source and arguments: opening task 8 after task 7 runs task 8's title
# query and shares the count both read, and opening the same address again
# runs nothing. A write outside the read set leaves the data current; a write
# that meets it makes it stale and the next open refetches it. Once the last
# screen that read a binding leaves, the registry drops it, so the board
# holds only the count and returning to task 8 fetches its title again. The
# same lines print at O0, O1 and O2 and under node on web.
fixture: RouteDataLifecycle.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
step o0: jet run -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = route_data_lifecycle.stdout.expected
step o1: jet run -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
step o2: jet run -O2 main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
when tool node
step: jet build --target web main.jet
exit: 0
step web: node app.js
cwd: .jet/build
exit: 0
stdout: == o0
end when
